    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4670A\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing a tax check-off\nfor the state library system\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the tax law to add a new section 630-i, Gifts for State Library\nSystem, to allow New York Taxpayers to contribute to the state library\naid program for financial support of public libraries.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFunding for the State Library Aid Program provides support for public\nlibraries and library systems, reference and research library resource\nsystems, the New York Public Research Libraries, the Schomburg\nCollection and the library for the Blind and Visually Handicapped. In\naddition, the aid program also provides special library incentives for\nacademic libraries, health information and hospital libraries, institu-\ntional libraries and the preservation of library resources. The State\nLibrary Aid Program is designed to provide solid financial assistance to\npublic libraries for the purposes of maintaining and improving the\nlibrary services of the state. However, in recent years state funding\nfor this program has remained relatively constant and has not kept pace\nfor the real needs of New York's libraries. This legislation would bring\nadditional annual revenue to the Library Aid Program by allowing taxpay-\ners the option to contribute to the State Library Aid Program via a \"tax\ncheck off.\" Such contributions are to be made at the same time state\ntaxes are filed. This check-off is similar to the \"Gift to Wildlife\"\ncheck-off that currently appears on the state personal income tax form.\nBecause donations are made on a voluntary basis, this legislation will\nproduce no financial hardship for any taxpayer, yet it will serve to\nsignificantly increase the amount of financial support for the State\nLibrary Aid Program.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S.4150- REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2017-18: S.2430- REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2015-16: S.2886A- REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2013-14: S.3235A- REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2012: S.6207- REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2011: S.2312- Referred TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n2009-10: S.974 - Investigations and Government Operations\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
